  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "Microsoft AI Red Team (AIRT) found phi-4's behavior similar to the phi-3 family and flagged risky behaviors that further safety post-training then addressed.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "19",
        "pdfPage": 19,
        "quote": "Overall, AIRT found that the behavior\nof phi-4 was similar to that of the phi-3 family, but identified several risky behaviors that were addressed"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Greedy Coordinate Gradient (GCG) adversarial suffixes generated on phi-3-medium did not transfer to phi-4.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "19",
        "pdfPage": 19,
        "quote": "generated adversarial suffixes using the GCG algorithm [ZWC+ 23] on phi-3-medium, but found that\nthese suffixes did not transfer to phi-4."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Authors state further red teaming is still needed across a broader range of scenarios and harm categories.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "19",
        "pdfPage": 19,
        "quote": "Further red teaming is required to identify possible risks across\na broader range of scenarios and harm categories."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "phi-4 can still invent biographies for plausible names, so factual hallucinations are not eliminated.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "20",
        "pdfPage": 20,
        "quote": "specifically in hallucinations around factual\nknowledge. For example, if X is a plausible human name, the model sometimes responds to prompts of the"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Responsible AI (RAI) mitigation reduced but did not fully resolve bias amplification, inappropriate content, and safety issues.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "20",
        "pdfPage": 20,
        "quote": "have resulted in mitigating\nthese issues across all dimensions, but have not resolved the issues completely."
      }
    }
  ],
